{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01085",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 2.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "good afternoon doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 3.92,
      "end_seconds": 8.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "not at all, please sit what seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.05,
      "end_seconds": 16.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "doctor, you know, I'm just here to help with the details"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.85,
      "end_seconds": 21.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Yes that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 22.12,
      "end_seconds": 26.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "ah, she's been having a pounding headache, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.79,
      "end_seconds": 29.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.78,
      "end_seconds": 39.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "hm. It was either the end of last month or earlier than that. I couldn't tell you the date"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.93,
      "end_seconds": 49.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.3,
      "end_seconds": 64.3,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "Loud noise definitely sets it off. It just comes and goes. I'd give it a eight, out of ten. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.23,
      "end_seconds": 67.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.77,
      "end_seconds": 75.9,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Vomiting goes along with it um most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.5,
      "end_seconds": 86.56,
      "duration_seconds": 10.06,
      "text": "Actually uh and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 86.66,
      "end_seconds": 92.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "tell the the doctor about the other thing that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.53,
      "end_seconds": 95.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.17,
      "end_seconds": 102.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "that's fine, one at a time i'll ask about everything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.84,
      "end_seconds": 108.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I've also had nausea, for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.89,
      "end_seconds": 112.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.35,
      "end_seconds": 120.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.82,
      "end_seconds": 122.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "how frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.68,
      "end_seconds": 126.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Honestly, all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.64,
      "end_seconds": 132.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.66,
      "end_seconds": 144.98,
      "duration_seconds": 10.32,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.38,
      "end_seconds": 150.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.33,
      "end_seconds": 162.18,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "ah I have high blood pressure for about ten years. I've never really been one for hospitals"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.7,
      "end_seconds": 163.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "mm, okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.54,
      "end_seconds": 170.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Anxiety, for about ten years. Migraines, for about a year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.82,
      "end_seconds": 178.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "Okay, I can see high blood pressure and anxiety in your file as well. Right, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.9,
      "end_seconds": 181.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.87,
      "end_seconds": 183.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "tell me your medicines please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 186.01,
      "end_seconds": 189.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Mm, she takes amlodipine, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.96,
      "end_seconds": 194.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 194.79,
      "end_seconds": 208.04,
      "duration_seconds": 13.25,
      "text": "it's 5 milligrams it's escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day, doctor so, it's sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed, doctor she takes Disprin, when it starts"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.57,
      "end_seconds": 211.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "how much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 212.91,
      "end_seconds": 214.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "325 milligrams"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.92,
      "end_seconds": 220.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Before this I was on propranolol; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.1,
      "end_seconds": 224.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.09,
      "end_seconds": 230.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.75,
      "end_seconds": 232.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.73,
      "end_seconds": 240.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.95,
      "end_seconds": 259.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.93,
      "end_seconds": 262.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.75,
      "end_seconds": 267.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "and what about loss of consciousness or neck stiffness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.25,
      "end_seconds": 284.31,
      "duration_seconds": 16.06,
      "text": "No, no loss of consciousness, no neck stiffness. I did have flashing lights before it starts at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.59,
      "end_seconds": 291.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "did you get slurred speech, weakness in the arms or legs or double vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.6,
      "end_seconds": 302.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "so you know I haven't had slurred speech weakness in the arms or legs or double vision no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.41,
      "end_seconds": 310.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.7,
      "end_seconds": 315.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "nothing on the the skin, um, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.53,
      "end_seconds": 319.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "how's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.17,
      "end_seconds": 322.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 326.16,
      "end_seconds": 336.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.75,
      "text": "Here are the the numbers, doctor. SpO2 97 percent on room air, temp 36.6 degrees, BP is 124 over 73, heart rate 84."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.49,
      "end_seconds": 338.19,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.25,
      "end_seconds": 341.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.52,
      "end_seconds": 344.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.65,
      "end_seconds": 365.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Cranial nerves look normal eye movements are full."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.86,
      "end_seconds": 369.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.82,
      "end_seconds": 387.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Power in all four limbs is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.0,
      "end_seconds": 391.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "tell me if that's sore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.38,
      "end_seconds": 402.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Neck is supple, no stiffness at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.38,
      "end_seconds": 427.65,
      "duration_seconds": 21.27,
      "text": "okay that's enough for me. From what you've told me and what I found my working impression is migraine with aura. Tension-type headache is still possible. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had a pounding headache and no loss of consciousness or slurred speech"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 432.06,
      "end_seconds": 434.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "yes, you've got it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 443.03,
      "end_seconds": 448.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "I'll request an MRI of the brain, it'll help with recurrent headaches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.69,
      "end_seconds": 452.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "that makes sense"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.11,
      "end_seconds": 487.23,
      "duration_seconds": 33.12,
      "text": "I'll start you on domperidone, 10 milligrams, when nauseous, as needed. You take it by mouth. It's for migraine nausea. Try not to skip meals and keep your sleep regular. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. The thing that would worry me is if you have the worst headache of your life or any weakness. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like you back in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 489.03,
      "end_seconds": 491.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 492.71,
      "end_seconds": 495.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "alright, thanks, take care"
    }
  ]
}